# ld-insights Architecture

## Overview
A React + Vite + Tailwind CSS v3 dashboard for Learning & Development analytics. Design tokens are sourced from Google Stitch MCP (`stitch.googleapis.com/mcp`). The Stitch project is `projects/11710553690432211807` (Learning Progress & Intervention System).

## Folder Structure
```
src/
  components/       # Shared layout shells only
    Layout.jsx      # Outlet wrapper — TopNav + SideNav + <main>
    TopNav.jsx      # Fixed header: logo, search, notifications, avatar
    SideNav.jsx     # Fixed sidebar: nav links, company block, Add Intervention CTA
  pages/            # One file per route; no nested folders
    Dashboard.jsx
    AtRisk.jsx
    EmployeeProfile.jsx
    Interventions.jsx
    Rules.jsx
    Reporting.jsx
    SessionPlanner.jsx
    Settings.jsx
    Help.jsx
  App.jsx           # BrowserRouter + all <Route> definitions
  main.jsx          # ReactDOM.createRoot entry
  index.css         # Tailwind directives only + .material-symbols-outlined base style
```

## Routing
All routes are children of the `<Layout />` component in `App.jsx`.

| Path | Component |
|---|---|
| `/` | Dashboard |
| `/at-risk` | AtRisk |
| `/at-risk/:id` | EmployeeProfile |
| `/interventions` | Interventions |
| `/rules` | Rules |
| `/reporting` | Reporting |
| `/sessions` | SessionPlanner |
| `/settings` | Settings |
| `/help` | Help |

## Adding a New Page
1. Create `src/pages/MyPage.jsx`
2. Add `<Route path="my-path" element={<MyPage />} />` inside the Layout route in `App.jsx`
3. Add a nav item to `SideNav.jsx` `navItems` array with `{ icon, label, to }`

## Key Dependencies
- `react-router-dom` — routing
- `tailwindcss@3` — styling via design tokens
- No component library — all UI is handcrafted with Tailwind classes
- No charting library — SVG and CSS-based charts only
- Material Symbols Outlined — icons loaded from Google Fonts in `index.html`
